## Data

### Camel Morph MSA v1.0 (morphological database)

- Source: https://github.com/CAMeL-Lab/camel_morph, file
  `official_releases/lrec-coling2024_release/databases/camel-morph-msa/camel_morph_msa_v1.0.db`,
  pinned to commit `15f5aede4b609db54abd6f87aded1f5ec5d930af`, SHA-256
  `110e03baa282874062d076e23d9671e985b6f76520b891d58cba4e55de0b8f60`
  (84,959,404 bytes). The commit, path and SHA-256 are fixed in
  `tools/parity/fetch_db.py`, which fetches and verifies the file; the same
  SHA-256 travels in each compiled asset's manifest.
- License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) for the
  data. The repository README's "Data License" section states (re-read
  2026-10-13 at the pinned commit, which was then also the head of `main`):
  "The data files accessed through the below links are licensed under a
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License." The first link
  below that sentence is this `.db` file (README.md lines 46 and 49 at the
  pin). The LREC-COLING 2024 release's own README and
  `official_releases/lrec-coling2024_release/databases/README.md` make the
  same statement for the release's databases. The repository's code
  is MIT (Copyright 2018-2022 New York University Abu Dhabi; reproduced
  verbatim at `licenses/CAMEL_MORPH_LICENSE`) and is not used by shanisarf.
- What shanisarf takes: the database, compiled into shanisarf's asset format
  (an adaptation under CC BY 4.0). The raw file is never committed; `tools/`
  downloads it to the git-ignored `data/`.
- Provenance of the scores: the stems' `lex_logprob` and `pos_lex_logprob`
  values are compiled in as published. Upstream computed them from Penn
  Arabic Treebank data synchronized with SAMA/MADA, resources of the
  Linguistic Data Consortium (LDC) that it says are not publicly accessible,
  and published the resulting values (a log-probability per lemma and per
  lemma-and-part-of-speech, 442 distinct values each; no text) in this file
  under CC BY 4.0 (`official_releases/lrec-coling2024_release/README.md` at
  the pin: the "Generating a DB" section, and the license line above it,
  which covers the file). shanisarf is not a party to any LDC agreement and
  relies on the licensor's statement, as it does for the rest of the file;
  the values carry no text and are committed nowhere (the parity fixtures
  that hold them are git-ignored). The `stripLogprobs` compile option sets
  them to `-99` for a caller's own build and says so in that asset's
  disclaimer.
- Obligation: attribution, in this file, in the README, and in the compiled
  asset's manifest (`credits` field), with a link to the license, a note
