### Camel Morph MSA v1.0 typed features (`src/msa-features.ts`, generated)

- Source: the Camel Morph MSA v1.0 database above, at the same commit and
  SHA-256; no separate download. `scripts/gen-msa-features.mjs` reads the
  git-ignored text under `data/` (its SHA-256 checked against
  `packages/shanisarf-db-msa/source.json`), or the compiled Asset when the
  text is absent, and writes the module (`npm run gen:features`).
- License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), the
  same license as the database the values are taken from. The module's code
  around them (its types and the `isMsaValue` guard) is shanisarf's, MIT.
- What shanisarf takes: the database's `ORDER` list (53 feature names) and
  the value lists of its 23 closed `DEFINE` lines (`pos`, `gen`, `num`,
  `enc0` and the others), in the database's order, as constants and types.
  No stem, gloss, score or other entry data; no text. The module is
  committed and ships in the core package, exported from the package root.
- Obligation: attribution, as for the database. The module's header names
  the Generator, the pin (name, version, commit and SHA-256) and the
  attribution text below with the license link, and points to this file.
- Attribution text: as for "Camel Morph MSA v1.0" above: "Camel Morph MSA
  v1.0, developed by the CAMeL Lab at New York University Abu Dhabi
  (Khairallah et al., 2024), https://github.com/CAMeL-Lab/camel_morph,
  licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  Adapted (compiled) by shanisarf."

## Fixture word lists

Each list added for parity fixtures gets a row here: source URL, license
(public domain / CC0 / CC BY only for committed fixtures), the derivation
applied, and the attribution text. A CC BY-SA list used only for a local
test from `data/` gets a row too, marked "local only, nothing committed".

The three lists below are built by `tools/parity/wordlists.py`, each
deterministically from the seed recorded in its own file header, and written
to `fixtures/wordlists/<name>.words.txt`.

### db-forms (parity word list)

- Source: derived from the Camel Morph MSA v1.0 database (see "Camel Morph
  MSA v1.0" above), not from any separate download.
- License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), the
  same license as the database it is sampled from.
- What shanisarf takes: a seeded sample of 1,200 stem surfaces, each as the
  bare stem and in up to three affixed forms chosen through the AB, BC and AC
  compatibility tables, plus one normalization variant per form where
  applicable. The list is generated at `tools/parity/generate.py` time from
  the git-ignored database; the resulting `fixtures/wordlists/db-forms.words.txt`
  is a committed CC BY 4.0 fixture.
- Obligation: attribution, as for the database. Attribution text: "Word
  forms sampled from Camel Morph MSA v1.0, developed by the CAMeL Lab at New
  York University Abu Dhabi (Khairallah et al., 2024),
  https://github.com/CAMeL-Lab/camel_morph, licensed under CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Sampled by shanisarf."

### edge-cases (parity word list)

- Source: invented by shanisarf; no third-party source.
- License: not applicable (original work; released with the repository under
  its MIT terms as a committed fixture).
- What shanisarf takes: nothing third-party. The list is an invented edge
  inventory (digits in
  three scripts, mixed script, tatweel, isolated diacritics, attached
  punctuation, empty and whitespace input, hamza and wasla forms, Persian
  letters, Latin/Cyrillic/CJK, a URL-like token, `NOAN`, ZWNJ, an emoji
  attached to Arabic, a supplementary-plane character), built without the
  database.
- Obligation: none (no third-party input). No running text; the list carries
  only invented or database-origin tokens and passes `scan_text.py`.

### backoff-nonwords (parity word list)

- Source: invented by shanisarf; no third-party source.
- License: not applicable (original work; committed fixture as above).
- What shanisarf takes: nothing third-party. 200 seeded strings generated
  over `AR_LETTERS_CHARSET` and filtered, at `generate.py` time, to those
  absent from the database's stem table, so each is a non-word that exercises
  the backoff path.
- Obligation: none (no third-party input). No running text.

## Generation request lists

Two request lists drive the generator and reinflector fixtures. They are
built by
`tools/parity/wordlists.py`, each deterministically from the seed recorded
in its own header line, and written to
`fixtures/wordlists/<name>.requests.jsonl`, one JSON object per line
(`lemma` or `word`, and `feats`). `tools/parity/scan_text.py` checks every
line's shape and string values before commit.

### gen-requests (parity request list)

- Source: derived from the Camel Morph MSA v1.0 database (see "Camel Morph
  MSA v1.0" above), plus invented edge requests; no separate download.
- License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), the
  same license as the database the lemmas and feature values are taken from.
- What shanisarf takes: a seeded sample of 300 lemmas of the database's
  lemma table, each with up to nine feature requests built from its first
  stem, its part of speech's `DEFAULTS` row and the database's defined values,
  one seeded clitic request each, and an invented block of edge requests (an
  unknown lemma, lemma suffixes, an undefined feature, an invalid value, a
  missing or undefined `pos`, a key outside the `DEFAULTS` row, the `NOAN`
  lemma). The list is generated at `tools/parity/generate.py` time from the
  git-ignored database; the resulting
  `fixtures/wordlists/gen-requests.requests.jsonl` is a committed CC BY 4.0
  fixture.
- Obligation: attribution, as for the database. Attribution text: "Lemmas
  and feature values sampled from Camel Morph MSA v1.0, developed by the
  CAMeL Lab at New York University Abu Dhabi (Khairallah et al., 2024),
  https://github.com/CAMeL-Lab/camel_morph, licensed under CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Sampled by shanisarf."

### reinflect-requests (parity request list)

- Source: the `db-forms` and `edge-cases` parity word lists above, with
  feature bundles invented by shanisarf.
- License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) for the
  `db-forms` words (derived from the database); the `edge-cases` words and
  the bundles are invented, with no third-party source.
- What shanisarf takes: 400 seeded `db-forms` words, each paired with ten
  invented feature bundles; every `edge-cases` word paired with three of
  them; and invented error bundles (an undefined feature, an invalid value,
  `ANY` on a feature that does not accept it).
- Obligation: attribution for the `db-forms` words, as for `db-forms`. No
  running text; every word passes `scan_text.py`.
